%%%
# A mixture of two bivariate normals

Spec §06 `ksuperpose` passes the parameter family with ONE FAMILY AXIS PER
COLLECTION ARGUMENT: "an argument's family axes are its leading axes in
excess of the rank (number of axes) of the parameter it feeds, and any
count other than one is a static error", and within the family the
same-number-of-axes requirement is suspended. So a `MvNormal` family takes
an N x d `mu` beside an N x d x d `cov`, and the mixture's variate is the
component variate — a vector of d.

This is the first suite row whose mixture components are MULTIVARIATE. The
two clusters carry distinct full covariances, so neither the `mu` axis nor
the `cov` axis can be dropped without moving the number.
%%%
flatppl_compat = "0.1"

mus = rowstack([[-2.0, 1.0], [3.0, -1.0]])
cA = rowstack([[1.0, 0.3], [0.3, 1.0]])
cB = rowstack([[0.5, 0.0], [0.0, 2.0]])
covs = [cA, cB]

w = [0.3, 0.7]

% Sum w = 1 already, so normalize only settles the static mass class.
mix = normalize(ksuperpose(MvNormal, w)(mu = mus, cov = covs))

y = elementof(cartpow(reals, 2))
